# Testing Standards

**Current state:** the repo has no test runner, no test files and no `npm test` script.
Verification today is `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npx next build` and the
`browser-qa` skill. Do not claim "tests pass" - say what you ran.

When tests are introduced, use this setup so every test file looks the same. For the
reasoning behind these rules read the `testing-principles` skill.

## Runner and setup (when adding tests)

- `vitest` + `happy-dom` + `@testing-library/react` + `@testing-library/user-event` +
  `@testing-library/jest-dom` as devDependencies; scripts `test` (`vitest run`) and
  `test:watch`.
- `vitest.config.ts` with `environment: "node"` as default and `vite-tsconfig-paths` so
  `@/*` resolves. DOM tests opt in per file with the first-line pragma
  `// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Do not use `jsdom`.
- Database code is never hit by unit tests: mock `@/lib/prisma` with `vi.mock` or test
  the pure parts of a service.

## What to test here (highest value first)

- Pure utils: `utils/formatting.ts` (currency, dates in `ru`, bonus pluralisation),
  `utils/validation.ts`, `utils/conversion.ts`, `utils/apiUtils/bonus.ts` (bonus split).
- Service business rules with Prisma mocked: bonus amounts (`REGISTRATION_BONUS`,
  `PERCENTAGE_FROM_FRIEND_PURCHASE`), purchase status transitions, DTOs stripping
  `password`.
- Hooks with `renderHook` + `act`: `useWindowDimensions`, `useAuthorizedRoute` (router
  mocked), `useBonusToPayConsultation`.
- RTK endpoints: assert the `query` builder output (url, method, body), not the fetch.
- Component tests only for behavior with real user value (form validation messages in
  `LoginModal`, empty vs filled `BonusList`). No snapshot tests of markup.

## File placement and naming

- Co-located: `utils/formatting.ts` -> `utils/formatting.test.ts`;
  `app/_components/Modal/LoginModal.tsx` -> `LoginModal.test.tsx`.
- No `__tests__` folders, no `.spec` files.

## Structure and style

```ts
// @vitest-environment happy-dom   <- only when the DOM is needed
import { describe, expect, it, vi } from "vitest";

describe("formatBonusPlural", () => {
  describe("when the amount ends in 1", () => {
    it("returns the singular form", () => {
      expect(formatBonusPlural(21)).toBe("21 балл");
    });
  });
});
```

- `describe` = unit or `when <condition>`; `it` starts with a verb (`returns`, `throws`,
  `shows`, `does not`). No "should".
- Test behavior and results, not implementation: no asserting on internal state or on
  mock call counts unless the call _is_ the behavior (e.g. "sends the email once").
- Use `user-event` over `fireEvent`; query by role/label text (Russian labels, e.g.
  `getByLabelText("Электронная почта")`); `findBy*` for async instead of
  `waitFor(() => getBy*)`.
- Mocks: `vi.mock` before importing the module under test; `vi.clearAllMocks()` in
  `beforeEach`; never mock `react-hook-form`, the shared inputs, or first-party hooks -
  mock the boundary (`@/lib/prisma`, `next/navigation`, `fetch`).
- Timers: `vi.useFakeTimers()` in `beforeEach`, `vi.useRealTimers()` in `afterEach`;
  compute time-dependent inputs _outside_ `renderHook`; wrap `advanceTimersByTime` in `act`.
- Attach `expect(promise).rejects` before triggering the rejection.

## Edge cases to cover

Boundary values (exact thresholds such as 20% bonus cap), `null` and `undefined`
separately, empty strings/arrays/zero, cleanup on unmount, error paths (expected `ApiError`
vs unexpected), loading -> success/error transitions.

## Never

- `.only` / `.skip` left in committed tests; console noise in passing tests.
- Deleting or weakening a test to make a check pass.
- Tests that hit the real Postgres database or send real email.
